# config/jev-prod-monitor - opt-in production Jev verdict poll
# (bin/fm-jev-prod-check.sh). Copy this into a local, gitignored
# config/jev-prod-monitor and edit. One `<key>:<value>` directive per non-empty,
# non-comment line, split on the FIRST colon.
#
# `repo` is the only required directive and names the project whose merged pull
# requests this home follows, as `<owner>/<repo>`. Exactly one is allowed: a
# second is refused rather than one of them being picked.
#
# `lookback-hours` is optional (default 48, range 1..336) and bounds how far back
# a merged pull request is still examined. A pull request older than it is never
# read again, which is what stops this poll growing without limit.
#
# `recorder-login` is optional and defaults to `github-actions[bot]`: the
# identity the check lane posts its verdict comment as. Only that author's
# marker comment counts as a verdict, because anybody who can comment on a pull
# request can write the marker. Set it only for a project whose lane posts under
# a different name.
#
# An ABSENT config/jev-prod-monitor means the feature is off: `check` stays
# completely silent, contacts no forge, and `arm` refuses. This file's mere
# presence is the opt-in.
#
# Arm the poll once per home with:
#
#   bin/fm-jev-prod-check.sh arm
#
# docs/configuration.md owns this schema. The `bearings` skill's "Jev production
# verdict follow-up" section owns what firstmate does with each class of wake.
repo:metaplanet-jp/core
lookback-hours:48
